WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.800
Hey, David, are anti Trump Republicans sort
of a third party now?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.690
Will they become a formal third party going
forward?

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.820
My instinct is no.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.280
And I know that a lot of you have been following
very closely groups like the Lincoln Project,

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.460
which are made up mostly of disaffected Republicans
who believe that the Republican Party under

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:23.039
Donald Trump is not really the Republican
Party of pre Donald Trump, which is true in

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:25.100
many senses.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.369
And could this split off?

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:29.910
Could this permanently fracture the Republican
Party?

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:30.910
I think the answer is no.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.360
And it's no for a couple of different reasons.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:39.110
Number one, if the Republican Party for more
formally fractures and you've got.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:44.200
Sort of like the Trumpy and Republicans and
then more traditional pre pre Trump Republicans.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.550
It helps Democrats dramatically because it
splits the right wing vote.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.550
Republicans know this.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.850
And so it would be dealing a huge amount of
self-inflicted damage if the Democratic Party

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:53.850
doesn't split.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.010
A split in the Republican Party.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.840
Destroys the possibilities of many Republicans
from getting reelected.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.440
So on a practical level, I don't think they're
going to do it.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:07.400
But there is another reason, which is that
until I see evidence otherwise, these groups

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:12.860
like the Lincoln Project and other anti Trump
Republicans, Mitt Romney, etc., this is temporary.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.260
If Biden wins, things go back to the way they
were in terms of their opposition to Democratic

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:23.230
policy, Democratic ideas, even when the Democratic
ideas are only marginally more left than the

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:28.600
mainstream Republican ideas as they are in
some cases, the Lincoln Project is a it's

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:36.800
a pre Trump Republican Party, and that means
that it is immediately going to go back to

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.310
saying what Joe Biden wants to do is bad.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.560
Joe Biden building a climate proposal on the
green New Deal is bad.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.590
Joe Biden wanting to uncap Social Security
earnings and eliminate the stepped up basis

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.270
clause and all of that.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.840
They're against all of that stuff.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:02:00.420
And so but my my belief is that this ends
as soon as soon as Donald Trump is out of

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.420
office.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.520
Now, there's one sort of caveat to this.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:11.379
A lot of these anti Trump Republicans have
said they aren't going to go back to the Republican

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:17.200
Party, that the idea being they've burnt their
bridges, that by opposing Donald Trump, they've

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:23.569
also ruined relationships with some of the
more traditional mainstream Republicans who

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:26.540
are falling in line with Trump and that that's
an irreparable relationship.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.540
No.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.959
One, history tells us otherwise.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:37.750
Politics makes strange bedfellows, grudges
that seem an unforgivable, so to speak.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:42.940
End up being forgiven either explicitly or
implicitly, and those same alliances end up

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.940
being formed.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:48.069
So I just don't believe that the the bridges
have been burned permanently.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.029
The bridges can be rebuilt.

00:02:50.029 --> 00:02:56.980
But number two, you can be out of the Republican
Party in some kind of strict technical sense

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:03.079
and still oppose Democrats and still end up
voting for future Republican candidates.

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:07.400
So it's partly that I don't believe them,
but partly it's it could be a technicality

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.840
now in terms of my view.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.230
I would love multiple parties and I would
love a different voting system.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.299
I've said before.

00:03:15.299 --> 00:03:21.879
The best path to empowering parties other
than Republicans and Democrats in the United

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:26.499
States involves serious campaign finance reform,
number one.

00:03:26.499 --> 00:03:31.310
And number two, a different voting system
than first past the post, because for as long

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.529
as we continue to have Purt first past the
post, the spoiler effect of supporting a third

00:03:36.529 --> 00:03:38.599
party candidate is too great.

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:41.900
If I love the Green Party.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.610
And then would vote Democratic.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.650
And really don't want a Republican, I risk
putting the Republican in office by voting

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.400
for the Green Party if on the right.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.709
I am actually so I don't know some far right
neo-Nazi.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:56.700
And I want David Duke.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:55.190
But if it's not David Duke, I'd prefer Trump.

